  "name": "Baakisimba (Kiganda dance-drumming)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Central dance-music of the Baganda of central Uganda, said to have begun at the royal court and now performed at ceremonies, celebrations and by cultural troupes. A large baakisimba drum, a small nankasa drum beaten with sticks and the long engalabi lead the ensemble, often joined by the endingidi tube fiddle and singing, while dancers move the waist and hips to the drums. The stick-beaten drum card stands in for the nankasa and the membrane-drum card for the baakisimba and empuunyi drums.",
